The classical bound for a transportation problem is m + n augmentations, one for each supply or demand that gets saturated. That bound does not hold here: by complementary slackness every arc carrying flow has reduced cost exactly zero, so its reverse arc is free to walk, and a shortest path can saturate one of those instead of a supply or a demand. How far past the bound it goes is a measurement, and ORC_Probe_Solver.mq5 is what takes it.
